WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.003 --> 00:00:06.492
My name is Maia, and I am a 47-year-old midwife living in Rome.

2
00:00:06.493 --> 00:00:11.378
Midwives are women who assist other women during childbirth.

3
00:00:11.379 --> 00:00:17.807
Midwifery is a profession that has been practiced since human families have been having children.

4
00:00:17.808 --> 00:00:23.006
My mother taught me how to be a midwife, and she taught me well.

5
00:00:23.007 --> 00:00:27.874
Giving birth is a joyous event, but it can be dangerous.

6
00:00:27.875 --> 00:00:36.522
So a midwife must, with the help of the gods, make sure the mother and her child are healthy and safe.

7
00:00:36.523 --> 00:00:46.707
In 146 BC Roman soldiers destroyed the Greek city of Corinth, made my mother a slave, and took her to Rome.

8
00:00:46.708 --> 00:00:53.585
Romans respect Greek science, and Greek midwives like my mother are well trained.

9
00:00:53.586 --> 00:01:01.823
When my mother settled in Rome in her master's house, he allowed her to work as a midwife for other families.

10
00:01:01.824 --> 00:01:06.885
She was paid well, so my mother was able to save some money.

11
00:01:06.886 --> 00:01:10.739
Soon she was able to buy her freedom.

12
00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:16.845
From age nine, I accompanied my mother to every birth and learned the craft.

13
00:01:16.846 --> 00:01:21.355
I discovered how women experience the birth of children.

14
00:01:21.356 --> 00:01:28.687
For example, it is natural for women to be fearful, especially when they are having their first child.

15
00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:35.210
Older mothers are more confident and understand that the pain eventually ends.

16
00:01:35.211 --> 00:01:41.372
But the first time I saw a birth, I became sick to my stomach.

17
00:01:41.373 --> 00:01:47.503
I had not expected such a large amount of blood, and the birth was very messy.

18
00:01:47.504 --> 00:01:51.920
The new mother cried so much that I cried too.

19
00:01:51.921 --> 00:01:59.534
My mother sternly told me that a good midwife must be calm in order to be a strong support for the mother.

20
00:01:59.535 --> 00:02:05.198
Even though there are some sad moments, being a midwife has many joys.

21
00:02:05.199 --> 00:02:09.322
So I am teaching my daughter Sofia this craft too.

22
00:02:09.323 --> 00:02:13.850
To be a good midwife, you should be able to read and write.

23
00:02:13.851 --> 00:02:23.015
When my mother was young, midwives learned mostly from experience, but now, midwives have some medical knowledge too.

24
00:02:23.016 --> 00:02:27.836
Hippocrates, the Greek physician, wrote a lot about women and their babies,

25
00:02:27.837 --> 00:02:36.738
and good midwives need to read and understand his ideas to deal with some of the problems that can arise during childbirth.

26
00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:47.958
Midwives also have to understand the nature of plants; for example, we need to know which herbs make labor and childbirth easier.

27
00:02:47.959 --> 00:02:55.019
One time a woman was in labor for over 12 hours, and the pain was almost unbearable.

28
00:02:55.020 --> 00:03:04.890
She became very tired and weak, so I made tea from the root of vervain, a plant with small purple flowers.

29
00:03:04.891 --> 00:03:13.632
When the mother drank this tea, it helped to speed up the delivery of her child, and her baby boy was born an hour later.

30
00:03:13.633 --> 00:03:21.517
Every woman should have a midwife when she is going to have a baby, but in Rome only wealthy women can hire one.

31
00:03:21.518 --> 00:03:28.180
When a woman first believes she is going to have a baby, she sends her slave to ask me to visit.

32
00:03:28.181 --> 00:03:34.574
Then I go to the woman's home to examine her body for signs that she will be a mother.

33
00:03:34.575 --> 00:03:43.281
I ask the woman many questions, and her answers help me determine when natal day—the day of birth—will be.

34
00:03:43.282 --> 00:03:48.599
Usually it takes about nine months for a baby to develop inside a woman.

35
00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:56.189
But every woman is different. Sometimes natal day comes a bit early and sometimes it is late.

36
00:03:56.190 --> 00:04:00.670
Even a midwife cannot know the exact day the baby will come.

37
00:04:00.671 --> 00:04:06.114
Most of the time, childbirth begins when the mother starts feeling labor spasms.

38
00:04:06.115 --> 00:04:12.496
Then a slave is sent to me, and I go quickly to the mother's home with two or three assistants.

39
00:04:12.497 --> 00:04:22.039
My daughter is one of them. Upon arrival we are taken into a room where the mother is lying in bed, usually in great pain.

40
00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:28.513
We bring soft strips of cloth, a pillow, herbs, and a special birthing chair.

41
00:04:28.514 --> 00:04:33.621
It is easier for mothers to give birth if they are sitting, rather than lying down.

42
00:04:33.622 --> 00:04:37.767
First we warm olive oil and water in pots.

43
00:04:37.768 --> 00:04:45.705
My assistants soak the soft cloths in water and then fold them against the woman's sides as she lies in bed.

44
00:04:45.706 --> 00:04:50.944
I massage the mother's belly and hips with warm olive oil too.

45
00:04:50.945 --> 00:04:58.543
The warmth eases the pain. Childbirth may take a few hours or last as long as a few days.

46
00:04:58.544 --> 00:05:02.972
But midwives always stay until the baby arrives.

47
00:05:02.973 --> 00:05:10.582
When the baby is ready to be born, my assistants and I carefully move the mother to the birthing chair.

48
00:05:10.583 --> 00:05:17.700
This chair has a wooden back and armrests that the mother can hold on to during the delivery.

49
00:05:17.701 --> 00:05:24.565
The seat is carved in the shape of a crescent moon so I can easily catch the baby when it comes out.

50
00:05:24.566 --> 00:05:31.237
My assistants hold the mother's shoulders and arms, and I bend down between the mother's legs.

51
00:05:31.238 --> 00:05:38.142
When I see the head of the baby coming out, I quickly wrap my hands in cloth or thin papyrus.

52
00:05:38.143 --> 00:05:47.995
I do this to make sure the baby does not slip out of my grasp. Finally the baby is born.

53
00:05:47.996 --> 00:05:52.441
Before giving the baby to the mother, I make sure it is healthy.

54
00:05:52.442 --> 00:05:58.169
I check the baby's arms and legs and count all the fingers and toes.

55
00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:01.659
A loud cry means the baby is strong.

56
00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:08.159
I also press a finger against the baby's skin to see if the baby is sensitive to touch.

57
00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:12.328
Then I cut the umbilical cord with a piece of pottery.

58
00:06:12.329 --> 00:06:21.993
After giving the baby a nice warm bath, I wrap it in a soft wool blanket, put it on a pillow, and give the baby to its mother.

59
00:06:21.994 --> 00:06:27.552
It is a Roman custom for the mother to then put the newborn on the floor.

60
00:06:27.553 --> 00:06:34.887
The father comes into the room and lifts the baby up to announce the new member of his family.

61
00:06:34.888 --> 00:06:49.291
I enjoy helping women give birth. There is no greater joy and satisfaction than seeing a new life enter this world.

